                                "sense_id": "959866ce-61b8-3c29-b276-4996ecfd41e8",
                                "text": "Night after night we cheerfully drank, squinting there in the dark like bulb-eyed lemurs, and once or twice even got toasted, waking up the next day on a dark, cold morning with the numbed, palsied tongue of dead vodka."
